  "tradeOffExplanation": "The note supplies three adopted outcomes and a changed-data success condition but no prerequisites, assessment structure or readiness evidence, so the plan books a single small end-to-end build-and-demonstrate activity (about 60-150 minutes, split at 45 minutes to fit the 60-minute daily ceiling) rather than separate preparatory lessons. This keeps the first useful checkpoint achievable early while leaving later engineering, tooling and project milestones as strategic, unbooked scope until the checkpoint is independently demonstrated. No official syllabus, assessment weighting or prerequisite sequence is assumed."
}

