            "instructions": "Retrieve your last check: five changed circuits, four wrong. For each of the five problems, write: (1) the circuit topology and given values; (2) the method you used; (3) the method that would have been applicable and why (state its assumptions and whether they hold for this circuit); (4) the specific error type: wrong method choice, wrong assumption, topology misread, or algebra/arithmetic slip; (5) the correct answer if you can now determine it. Use only methods actually taught in your course; if a problem required a method you have not been taught, mark it 'untaught method' rather than guessing. Produce a numbered list of the five problems with these five items each. Do not re-solve all five from scratch yet; this is diagnosis only.",
