            "instructions": "Using the error list from diagnose_errors, group the failures by method category. For each failing category, work through two changed problems (different from the original five) that use circuits of the same type. For each problem: (1) state the circuit topology and values; (2) state which taught methods are applicable and check each method's assumptions against this circuit; (3) select one applicable method and justify the selection; (4) solve step by step, showing the algebra; (5) check the answer by an independent route (e.g., a different applicable method, or unit/limiting-case check) and state whether it agrees. If a category required an untaught method, mark it as an unresolved gap and do not attempt it. If diagnosis found no failures in a category, skip it. Write each solution fully; do not just state final answers.",
